{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take Aaron, etc.</b> This passage was stated before the erection of the Mishkan, and the reason it was stated here is to tell you that all the laws of the offerings and their details and their precise rules preceded his consecration, for in order to perform all of them he and his sons were consecrated, and he was not consecrated until Moses taught him all the specific laws of every offering and he undertook and accepted upon himself to do everything written, and only then did He say to him ״קַח אֶת אַהֲרֹן״ — for on this condition he was consecrated. Further, without this one would find that a person from Israel might bring an offering immediately upon drawing near before HaShem and not know what to do."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:09.189648016Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}